Section 1 manual pages for FUZIX
================================

`man' (Applications/util/man.c) reads pages from /usr/man/man<N>/ in the
nroff -man subset that program understands: .TH .SH .SS .PP .TP .IP .RS
.RE .B .I .BI .BR .IB .IR .RB .RI .nf .fi .br .sp and \" comments.  It
is not nroff: it has no macro definitions (.de), no .ti, no .ds, and it
prints a visible "**** Unknown formatter command" line into the middle
of the page for anything else.

Kernel/platform/platform-rpipico/manpages.sh is the gate: it builds
man.c for the host, renders every page here and fails on that line;
checks the built card image for a command with no page or a page naming
no command; and checks that every SEE ALSO resolves.  Run it after
touching anything in this directory.

Other things man(1) does not have, all of which were tried and had to
come back out: .TQ, .ti, .ds, .ns, .de.  A line beginning with a bare
dot is read as a request, so an ed transcript needs \&. for its
terminator.  \(aq and its relatives all render as an asterisk, so use
plain quotes.  A literal backslash in the OUTPUT needs \\ in the
source; \e renders as nothing at all, because man eats a backslash
followed by any letter.

WHY THIS DIRECTORY EXISTS

The card carried one manual page - levee.1 - so `man awk' and `man sed'
answered "No manual entry".  The pages here fill that in for the rest of
what /bin holds.

WHERE PAGES COME FROM

  Applications/V7/cmd/*.1     the V7 originals, for the V7 binaries.
                              Installed from where they are; not copied.
  Applications/levee/levee.1  ditto, and it is `vi' here as well.
  Applications/util/man.1     ditto.
  Applications/awk/awk.1      upstream one-true-awk's page.  It uses
                              .de macros man(1) cannot do, so mkawk1.sh
                              converts it into awk.1 here.  The upstream
                              file is not touched, in keeping with
                              Applications/awk/PORTING.
  this directory              everything else, written from the source
                              of the binary that is actually installed.

WRITTEN FROM THE SOURCE, NOT FROM MEMORY

These are not Linux pages with the GNU options filed off.  Every option
listed here was read out of the .c file that builds the binary on the
card, and the divergences are the point: `rm' silently ignores -r,
`killall' takes no process name and kills everything, `ssh' is a shell
and not a remote login, `cat' has no options at all.  A page that
promises a flag the binary does not have is worse than no page, which is
the same rule mancheck.sh enforces for the manual.

Where a command has a NOTES section it is because the FUZIX binary
differs from what a hand trained on Linux or on V7 would expect.  Read
those first.

FOUR COMMANDS ARE INSTALLED TWICE

update-flash.sh bgets su, sum, ed and dd from Applications/util and then
again from Applications/V7/cmd.  The second write wins, so the V7 build
is what boots and the V7 page is what is installed.  Confirmed by
comparing on-card sizes against both candidates.
